pub fn topic_summary(i: i64) -> &'static [u8] {
    match i {
        0 => b"about 2k tokens: the language in one program (values, let mut, references, moves), std's most used items, first errors, the loop (the default)",
        1 => b"a whole program in three files and a test case: modules, enums and match, Result and ?, Vec, HashMap, Buf, sorting, allocators",
        2 => b"the long form of the core: values, functions, structs, generics, modules, slices, std, input, unsafe, errors, tools",
        3 => b"Rust -> vole, area by area: text, parameters and memory (&T, &mut T, let mut), errors, iteration, syntax",
        4 => b"lexical rules (Rust's, plus text blocks), items, statements, precedence, control flow, patterns",
        5 => b"float math (0.25.2.1): Rust's f32 and f64 methods (sqrt, sin, atan2, powi, min, ...), f64::consts::PI, f64::EPSILON; pure vole, no C; the integers' abs, min, max, clamp, signum, pow (0.25.2.2)",
        6 => b"numbers and their defined behaviour, arrays, slices, pointers, distinct types and NonNull (0.18), enums, SIMD",
        7 => b"Vec, HashMap, Buf, Option, Result, printing, reading stdin, text, sort: the API from std's source",
        8 => b"str and String: UTF-8 text with Rust's methods (split, trim, find, parse, lines, chars), patterns, the _in forms, bytes to text; string constants, as_bytes, format_in; numbers as text without an allocator (fmt::Write)",
        9 => b"files, paths, the environment, processes (0.20): std::fs, io::Error, BufReader, BufWriter, std::path, std::env, std::process",
        10 => b"command lines (0.24): std::cli, a Command of flags, options, positionals and subcommands; Matches; the help, errors with try: lines, exit codes",
        11 => b"Rust's ownership: Copy and move, borrowing (&T, &mut T) and the borrowck.* errors with rustc's codes, lifetimes, drops and Drop guards, slices, Cell",
        12 => b"allocation as a capability (0.16, 0.26.3): gpa from main, the _in forms, A: Allocator in types, arenas, unsafe impl, --check-alloc, fix --only alloc",
        13 => b"what a function may do (0.16): alloc(Gpa) io static panic diverge unsafe, query effects, #[pure] and its kin",
        14 => b"the errors newcomers hit, each with its fix; run-time failures",
        15 => b"files, mod, pub, use, paths, the prelude",
        16 => b"type parameters, instances, the turbofish, inference",
        17 => b"traits, impls, defaults, bounds, operator traits, supertraits, associated types and constants, blanket impls",
        18 => b"|x| x + k, what a closure captures, move closures, Fn, FnMut and FnOnce bounds, fn coercion, impl Fn results",
        19 => b"Iterator and Item, sources (iter, iter_mut, into_iter, ranges, HashMap), Rust's adapters and consumers, collect_in, sort_by, your own iterator",
        20 => b"integer casts and widening, From and Into, the ? operator, parse and its errors, reading stdin",
        21 => b"format strings and the spec, float text, Display and Debug, the print family, #[derive]",
        22 => b"unsafe operations, raw pointers and &x, unsafe fn, --check-unsafe",
        23 => b"calling C, importing headers, repr(C), callbacks, linking",
        24 => b"std::window (0.23): an App, windows, pulled events, keys, text and input methods, mouse (mapped with the surface's size), frames on request, the clipboard; when the window is not shown (timer frames, timing headless); the scale is the window's, not the surface's; checking the pixels headless (a PPM, 0.25.4)",
        25 => b"atomics, std::thread (spawn_in, scope), thread-locals, Send and Sync, the sync/thread/tls effects",
        26 => b"SIMD and CPU intrinsics (0.19): NEON, SSE, AVX2, CRC32, AES, SHA-256, popcount; finding one (query arch), byte search, detect and has, #[target_feature], #[multiversion], checked memory",
        27 => b"working on a GPU example, short: where a shader lives (embed wgsl, a .wgsl file), volec check validates the shader, build, the headless run (--headless --samples --size --out), sweeping a parameter without editing the shader, the examples' READMEs",
        28 => b"GPU compute and rendering (0.22): std::gpu on Metal, a skeleton (window, compute, render, readback), handles (which move; a struct, a Vec, closures), dispatch ordering, descriptors, buffer usages, surface, texture and storable formats, bind groups and layouts (a pipeline's own entry points), one module per kernel, index buffers (no indirect draws), uniform layout and gpu.unwritten, workgroups, buffer sizes and adapter.limits(), atomics, a compute simulation, ping-pong, per-step parameters, timing (latency, throughput), what the WGSL translation rejects, the gpu.* contracts",
        29 => b"GPU rendering (0.22): render to a texture, a textured quad (vertex layouts of several attributes, write_texture, samplers, textureSampleLevel), multiple render targets, depth-only passes; drawing over the image (an overlay: Load::Keep, Blend::alpha, text from an R8 atlas, 0.25.4)",
        30 => b"query, edit, refactor, fix, check, diagnostics and try lines",
        31 => b"requires, ensures, old and result, assert and assert_eq, debug clauses, the failure line (0.18)",
        32 => b"#[test] (with gpa: Gpa; it sees its module's private items), a check must be able to fail, #[property] and Arbitrary, snapshots, volec test, #[fuzz] and volec fuzz, reduce over programs (0.18)",
        33 => b"a bug: tests with failure traces, probe values at a line, reduce an input, which change broke a test (0.17)",
        34 => b"recipes for \"add an X\": a std function, a peephole rule, a pass, a diagnostic, a test, a subcommand, a module (0.17)",
        35 => b"the style (0.25.1): imports grouped std, crate, the rest; 4 spaces, 100 columns, trailing commas; volec fmt --check",
        _ => b"",
    }
}

